---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI provides support for text-to-speech generation through dedicated TTS adapters. This guide covers how to convert text into spoken audio using OpenAI and Gemini providers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-speech (TTS) is handled by TTS adapters that follow the same tree-shakeable architecture as other adapters in TanStack AI. The TTS adapters support:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"text","value":": TTS-1, TTS-1-HD, and audio-capable GPT-4o models"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Gemini 2.5 Flash TTS (experimental)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BytePlus"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Seed Speech ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"seed-audio-1.0"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal.ai"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Kokoro, ElevenLabs, MiniMax, Chatterbox, Dia, Orpheus, F5-TTS, VibeVoice, and more"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Most providers here ship a fixed catalog of voices. When none of them fit, "},{"type":"link","href":"./voice-creation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"create your own"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and pass the new voice ID as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"},{"type":"text","value":". On a provider whose catalog is per-account, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listVoices()"},{"type":"text","value":" reads back what is available."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openai-text-to-speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI Text-to-Speech"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\n// Generate speech from text (uses OPENAI_API_KEY from environment)\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n  text: 'Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!',\n  voice: 'alloy',\n})\n\n// result.audio contains base64-encoded audio data\nconsole.log(result.format) // 'mp3'\nconsole.log(result.contentType) // 'audio/mpeg'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"gemini-text-to-speech-experimental","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini Text-to-Speech (Experimental)"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { geminiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n\n// Generate speech from text (uses GOOGLE_API_KEY or GEMINI_API_KEY from environment)\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: geminiSpeech('gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview'),\n  text: 'Hello from Gemini TTS!',\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.audio) // Base64 encoded audio","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fal-ai-text-to-speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal.ai Text-to-Speech"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal.ai offers a broad selection of TTS models, Google's brand-new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-3.1-flash-tts"},{"type":"text","value":", ElevenLabs v3, MiniMax 2.6 HD, Kokoro's multilingual voices, and more. Pass the model ID as a string literal for fully typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\n// Google Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS, 80+ languages, expressive audio tags\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: falSpeech('fal-ai/gemini-3.1-flash-tts'),\n  text: '[warm, enthusiastic] Welcome to TanStack AI!',\n  voice: 'Kore',\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\n// Kokoro multilingual\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: falSpeech('fal-ai/kokoro/american-english'),\n  text: 'Hello from fal!',\n  voice: 'af_heart',\n  speed: 1.0,\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.audio) // Base64 encoded audio\nconsole.log(result.format) // e.g. \"wav\"","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\n// ElevenLabs v3 with model-specific options\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: falSpeech('fal-ai/elevenlabs/tts/eleven-v3'),\n  text: 'Welcome to TanStack AI.',\n  // The fal adapter maps top-level `voice`/`speed` into the model input;\n  // `modelOptions` is reserved for model-specific keys.\n  voice: 'Rachel',\n  modelOptions: {\n    stability: 0.5,\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"byteplus-seed-speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BytePlus Seed Speech"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Seed Speech is a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"separate BytePlus product from ModelArk"}]},{"type":"text","value":", so it uses its own key ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BYTEPLUS_VOICE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":") rather than the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ARK_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" the chat, image and video adapters read. Voice ids go on the wire as Seed Speech's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"speaker"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0'),\n  text: 'Welcome to TanStack AI!',\n  voice: 'en_female_stokie_uranus_bigtts',\n  format: 'mp3',\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.contentType) // \"audio/mpeg\"","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Formats are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wav"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mp3"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pcm"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ogg_opus"},{"type":"text","value":", and synthesis is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"capped at 120 seconds of output"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Seed Audio also does multi-role dialogue and word-level timings. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"turns"},{"type":"text","value":" for dialogue and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamps"},{"type":"text","value":" for timings, both covered below."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Seed Speech has no top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"speaker"},{"type":"text","value":" field: the adapter sends "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"},{"type":"text","value":" as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"references: [{ speaker }]"},{"type":"text","value":". Because "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.references"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"replaces"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that array rather than merging into it, passing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"references"},{"type":"text","value":" for voice cloning silently drops "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"},{"type":"text","value":" — include a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"speaker"},{"type":"text","value":" member yourself if you still want a stock voice. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/byteplus#text-to-speech-seed-speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BytePlus adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the voice-id naming conventions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"common-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All TTS adapters support these common options:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The text to convert to speech. Required unless you pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"turns"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"turns"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array<{ text, voice }>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dialogue lines, one per speaker turn. Use it instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The voice to use for generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Output audio format (e.g., \"mp3\", \"wav\")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamps"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ask for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alignment"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"segments"},{"type":"text","value":" on the result"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openai-voice-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI Voice Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI provides several distinct voices:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alloy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Neutral, balanced voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echo"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Warm, conversational voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expressive, storytelling voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onyx"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deep, authoritative voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nova"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Friendly, upbeat voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shimmer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear, gentle voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ash"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Calm, measured voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ballad"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Melodic, flowing voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"coral"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bright, energetic voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sage"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wise, thoughtful voice"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"verse"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Poetic, rhythmic voice"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openai-format-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI Format Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Format"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mp3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MP3 audio (default)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opus"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Opus audio (good for streaming)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aac"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AAC audio"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flac"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FLAC audio (lossless)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wav"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WAV audio (uncompressed)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pcm"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Raw PCM audio"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"dialogue-with-two-or-more-voices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dialogue With Two or More Voices"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want a two-person skit, and one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":" string with one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot give\nyou that. Prefixing speaker names into the string is a guess about the prompt\nformat, and the provider never tells you which line landed where."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"turns"},{"type":"text","value":" instead. Each turn carries its own text and its own voice:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\n// Replace SECOND_VOICE with another voice id from the BytePlus voice list.\nconst SECOND_VOICE = 'your-second-voice-id'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0'),\n  turns: [\n    {\n      text: 'Do you have a left-handed bass?',\n      voice: 'en_female_stokie_uranus_bigtts',\n    },\n    { text: 'We do. Come and try it.', voice: SECOND_VOICE },\n  ],\n  format: 'mp3',\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"turns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":" are mutually exclusive. Pass one or the other."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not every provider can do dialogue, and the ones that can have different\nspeaker limits. The adapter declares its limit, so a request that asks for too\nmany voices fails before it reaches the provider:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Distinct voices per request"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byteplusSpeech"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsSpeech"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"10"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"geminiSpeech"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other TTS adapters"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dialogue not supported"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the limit at runtime from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter.capabilities"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\nconst adapter = byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0')\n\nconsole.log(adapter.capabilities?.maxSpeakers) // 3\nconsole.log(adapter.capabilities?.timestamps) // true","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"timings-where-each-word-and-turn-lands","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Timings: Where Each Word and Turn Lands"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result.duration"},{"type":"text","value":" is the length of the file. It does not tell you where speech\nstops, and it does not tell you which turn is where. Trimming trailing silence\nor captioning a clip needs both."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamps: true"},{"type":"text","value":" and the result carries the timings:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0'),\n  text: 'Welcome to the guitar store.',\n  timestamps: true,\n})\n\n// Where speech ends, which is earlier than the end of the file.\nconst speechEnds = result.alignment?.endSeconds.at(-1)\n\nfor (const segment of result.segments ?? []) {\n  console.log(segment.startSeconds, segment.endSeconds, segment.text)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two fields come back, and they answer different questions:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alignment"},{"type":"text","value":": one entry per character or per word, with start and end times.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alignment.unit"},{"type":"text","value":" says which granularity the provider reported."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"segments"},{"type":"text","value":": one entry per turn (dialogue) or per sentence (single voice).\nA dialogue segment also carries "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"turnIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All times are seconds. Providers that report milliseconds convert in the\nadapter, so you never mix units."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timestamps"},{"type":"text","value":" is rejected on an adapter that cannot return timings, rather than\nsilently giving you a result with nothing in it. Check\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter.capabilities?.timestamps"},{"type":"text","value":" before you ask."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"playing-audio-in-the-browser","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Playing Audio in the Browser"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Convert base64 to audio and play\nfunction playAudio(result: TTSResult) {\n  const audioData = atob(result.audio)\n  const bytes = new Uint8Array(audioData.length)\n  for (let i = 0; i < audioData.length; i++) {\n    bytes[i] = audioData.charCodeAt(i)\n  }\n  \n  const blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: result.contentType })\n  const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)\n  \n  const audio = new Audio(url)\n  audio.play()\n  \n  // Clean up when done\n  audio.onended = () => URL.revokeObjectURL(url)\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"saving-audio-to-file-node-js","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Saving Audio to File (Node.js)"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { writeFile } from 'fs/promises'\n\nasync function saveAudio(result: TTSResult, filename: string) {\n  const audioBuffer = Buffer.from(result.audio, 'base64')\n  await writeFile(filename, audioBuffer)\n  console.log(`Saved to ${filename}`)\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n  text: 'Hello world!',\n})\n\nawait saveAudio(result, 'output.mp3')","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"full-stack-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full-Stack Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI provides React hooks and server-side streaming helpers to build full-stack text-to-speech with minimal boilerplate."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"streaming-mode-server-route-client-hook","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming Mode (Server Route + Client Hook)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server"}]},{"type":"text","value":", Create an API route that wraps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":" as a streaming response:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/api/generate/speech.ts\nimport { generateSpeech, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/generate/speech')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body = await request.json()\n        const { text, voice, format, model } = body.data\n\n        const stream = generateSpeech({\n          adapter: openaiSpeech(model ?? 'tts-1'),\n          text,\n          voice,\n          format,\n          stream: true,\n        })\n\n        return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client"}]},{"type":"text","value":", Use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":" hook with a connection adapter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateSpeech, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/speech'),\n  })\n\n  const playAudio = () => {\n    if (!result) return\n    const audioData = atob(result.audio)\n    const bytes = new Uint8Array(audioData.length)\n    for (let i = 0; i < audioData.length; i++) {\n      bytes[i] = audioData.charCodeAt(i)\n    }\n    const blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: result.contentType })\n    const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)\n    const audio = new Audio(url)\n    audio.play()\n    audio.onended = () => URL.revokeObjectURL(url)\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate Speech'}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n      {result && <button onClick={playAudio}>Play Audio</button>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The other two transports (a server function returning JSON, or one returning an\nSSE "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"},{"type":"text","value":") work the same way here. They are in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"#other-transports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced: other transports"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and explained once in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./generations#transports-in-full","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generations"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hook-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hook API"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useGenerateSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":" hook accepts:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ConnectionAdapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming transport (SSE, HTTP stream, custom)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetcher"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(input) => Promise<TTSResult | Response>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct async function, or server function returning an SSE "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(result) => TOutput | null | void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callback when audio is generated. Optionally return a transformed value (see "},{"type":"link","href":"#result-transform","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result Transform"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(error) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callback on error"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onProgress"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(progress, message?) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Progress updates (0-100)"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And returns:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generate"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(input: SpeechGenerateInput) => Promise<void>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trigger generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TOutput | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The result (or transformed result), or null"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether generation is in progress"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error | undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current error, if any"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationClientState"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'idle'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'generating'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'success'"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'error'"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Abort the current generation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear result, error, and return to idle"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"result-transform","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result Transform"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult"},{"type":"text","value":" callback can optionally return a transformed value that replaces the stored "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":". This is useful for converting raw API responses into a more convenient format for your components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transform behavior:"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"non-null value"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to replace the stored result with the transformed value"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to keep the previous result unchanged (useful for filtering)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"nothing"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":") to store the raw result as-is (backward compatible)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: Convert base64 audio to a playable Audio element"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateSpeech, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport type { TTSResult } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nfunction SpeechPlayer() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/speech'),\n    onResult: (raw: TTSResult) => {\n      const audioData = atob(raw.audio)\n      const bytes = new Uint8Array(audioData.length)\n      for (let i = 0; i < audioData.length; i++) {\n        bytes[i] = audioData.charCodeAt(i)\n      }\n      const blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: raw.contentType })\n      const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)\n      return {\n        audio: new Audio(url),\n        duration: raw.duration,\n      }\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello world!', voice: 'alloy' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n      {result && (\n        <button onClick={() => result.audio.play()}>\n          Play Audio\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript automatically infers the result type from your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResult"},{"type":"text","value":" return value, no explicit generic parameter needed. In this example, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result"},{"type":"text","value":" is inferred as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ audio: HTMLAudioElement; duration?: number } | null"},{"type":"text","value":", so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result.audio.play()"},{"type":"text","value":" is fully type-safe."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"advanced","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reference detail you do not need to get this working."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"other-transports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other transports"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"direct-mode-server-function-fetcher","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct Mode (Server Function + Fetcher)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For non-streaming usage with TanStack Start server functions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport const generateSpeechFn = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .inputValidator((data: { text: string; voice?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    return generateSpeech({\n      adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n      text: data.text,\n      voice: data.voice,\n    })\n  })","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { generateSpeechFn } from '../lib/server-functions'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    fetcher: (input) => generateSpeechFn({ data: input }),\n  })\n  // ... same UI as above\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"server-function-streaming-fetcher-response","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Function Streaming (Fetcher + Response)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For TanStack Start server functions that stream results. The fetcher receives type-safe input and returns an SSE "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"},{"type":"text","value":", the client parses it automatically:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { generateSpeech, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport const generateSpeechStreamFn = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .inputValidator((data: { text: string; voice?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(({ data }) => {\n    return toServerSentEventsResponse(\n      generateSpeech({\n        adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n        text: data.text,\n        voice: data.voice,\n        stream: true,\n      }),\n    )\n  })","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"import { useGenerateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { generateSpeechStreamFn } from '../lib/server-functions'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    fetcher: (input) => generateSpeechStreamFn({ data: input }),\n  })\n  // ... same UI as above\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"openai-model-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI Model Options"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1-hd'),\n  text: 'High quality speech synthesis',\n  voice: 'nova',\n  format: 'mp3',\n  speed: 1.0, // top-level option, 0.25 to 4.0\n  modelOptions: {\n    instructions: 'Speak in a calm, measured tone', // GPT-4o audio models only\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"speed"},{"type":"text","value":" are top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":" options, not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" keys."}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instructions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice style instructions (GPT-4o audio models only)"}]}]]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instructions"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream_format"},{"type":"text","value":" options are only available with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-4o-audio-preview"},{"type":"text","value":" model, not with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tts-1"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tts-1-hd"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"response-format","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Response Format"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The TTS result includes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface TTSResult {\n  id: string        // Unique identifier for this generation\n  model: string     // The model used\n  audio: string     // Base64-encoded audio data\n  format: string    // Audio format (e.g., \"mp3\")\n  contentType: string // MIME type (e.g., \"audio/mpeg\")\n  duration?: number // Duration in seconds (if available)\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"model-availability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model Availability"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"openai-models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI Models"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quality"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Speed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Case"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tts-1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fast"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Real-time applications"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tts-1-hd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"High"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Slower"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production audio"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-4o-audio-preview"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Highest"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Variable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced voice control"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"gemini-models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini Models"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Status"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notes"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"May require Live API for full features"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"error-handling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\ntry {\n  const result = await generateSpeech({\n    adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n    text: 'Hello!',\n  })\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    if (error.message.includes('exceeds maximum length')) {\n      console.error('Text is too long (max 4096 characters)')\n    } else if (error.message.includes('Speed must be between')) {\n      console.error('Invalid speed value')\n    } else {\n      console.error('TTS error:', error.message)\n    }\n  }\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tip:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" To trigger speech generation from your frontend with loading states, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./generation-hooks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation Hooks"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" When a TTS request fails or produces unexpected output, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debug: true"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech({...})"},{"type":"text","value":" to log the outgoing request, every raw provider chunk, and any caught error. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/debug-logging","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug Logging"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"environment-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The TTS adapters use the same environment variables as other adapters:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GOOGLE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GEMINI_API_KEY"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BytePlus"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BYTEPLUS_VOICE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" (Seed Speech is a different product from ModelArk — the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ARK_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" used by the chat/image/video adapters is not accepted here)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"explicit-api-keys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit API Keys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For production use or when you need explicit control:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createOpenaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { createGeminiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n\n// OpenAI\nconst openaiAdapter = createOpenaiSpeech('tts-1', 'your-openai-api-key')\n\n// Gemini\nconst geminiAdapter = createGeminiSpeech('gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview', 'your-google-api-key')","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"best-practices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Best Practices"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text Length"}]},{"type":"text","value":": OpenAI TTS supports up to 4096 characters per request. For longer content, split into chunks."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice Selection"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Choose voices appropriate for your content—use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onyx"},{"type":"text","value":" for authoritative content, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nova"},{"type":"text","value":" for friendly interactions."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Format Selection"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mp3"},{"type":"text","value":" for general use, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opus"},{"type":"text","value":" for streaming, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wav"},{"type":"text","value":" for further processing."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caching"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Cache generated audio to avoid regenerating the same content."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Always handle errors gracefully, especially for user-facing applications."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"openai-text-to-speech","text":"OpenAI Text-to-Speech","level":3},{"id":"gemini-text-to-speech-experimental","text":"Gemini Text-to-Speech (Experimental)","level":3},{"id":"fal-ai-text-to-speech","text":"fal.ai Text-to-Speech","level":3},{"id":"byteplus-seed-speech","text":"BytePlus Seed Speech","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"common-options","text":"Common Options","level":3},{"id":"openai-voice-options","text":"OpenAI Voice Options","level":3},{"id":"openai-format-options","text":"OpenAI Format Options","level":3},{"id":"dialogue-with-two-or-more-voices","text":"Dialogue With Two or More Voices","level":2},{"id":"timings-where-each-word-and-turn-lands","text":"Timings: Where Each Word and Turn Lands","level":2},{"id":"playing-audio-in-the-browser","text":"Playing Audio in the Browser","level":2},{"id":"saving-audio-to-file-node-js","text":"Saving Audio to File (Node.js)","level":2},{"id":"full-stack-usage","text":"Full-Stack Usage","level":2},{"id":"streaming-mode-server-route-client-hook","text":"Streaming Mode (Server Route + Client Hook)","level":3},{"id":"hook-api","text":"Hook API","level":3},{"id":"result-transform","text":"Result Transform","level":3},{"id":"advanced","text":"Advanced","level":2},{"id":"other-transports","text":"Other transports","level":3},{"id":"direct-mode-server-function-fetcher","text":"Direct Mode (Server Function + Fetcher)","level":4},{"id":"server-function-streaming-fetcher-response","text":"Server Function Streaming (Fetcher + Response)","level":4},{"id":"model-options","text":"Model Options","level":3},{"id":"openai-model-options","text":"OpenAI Model Options","level":4},{"id":"response-format","text":"Response Format","level":3},{"id":"model-availability","text":"Model Availability","level":3},{"id":"openai-models","text":"OpenAI Models","level":4},{"id":"gemini-models","text":"Gemini Models","level":4},{"id":"error-handling","text":"Error Handling","level":3},{"id":"environment-variables","text":"Environment Variables","level":3},{"id":"explicit-api-keys","text":"Explicit API Keys","level":3},{"id":"best-practices","text":"Best Practices","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack AI provides support for text-to-speech generation through dedicated TTS adapters. This guide covers how to convert text into spoken audio using OpenAI and Gemini providers.\n\n## Overview\n\nText-to-speech (TTS) is handled by TTS adapters that follow the same tree-shakeable architecture as other adapters in TanStack AI. The TTS adapters support:\n\n- **OpenAI**: TTS-1, TTS-1-HD, and audio-capable GPT-4o models\n- **Gemini**: Gemini 2.5 Flash TTS (experimental)\n- **BytePlus**: Seed Speech (`seed-audio-1.0`)\n- **fal.ai**: Kokoro, ElevenLabs, MiniMax, Chatterbox, Dia, Orpheus, F5-TTS, VibeVoice, and more\n\nMost providers here ship a fixed catalog of voices. When none of them fit, [create your own](./voice-creation) and pass the new voice ID as `voice`. On a provider whose catalog is per-account, `listVoices()` reads back what is available.\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n### OpenAI Text-to-Speech\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\n// Generate speech from text (uses OPENAI_API_KEY from environment)\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n  text: 'Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!',\n  voice: 'alloy',\n})\n\n// result.audio contains base64-encoded audio data\nconsole.log(result.format) // 'mp3'\nconsole.log(result.contentType) // 'audio/mpeg'\n```\n\n### Gemini Text-to-Speech (Experimental)\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { geminiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n\n// Generate speech from text (uses GOOGLE_API_KEY or GEMINI_API_KEY from environment)\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: geminiSpeech('gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview'),\n  text: 'Hello from Gemini TTS!',\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.audio) // Base64 encoded audio\n```\n\n### fal.ai Text-to-Speech\n\nfal.ai offers a broad selection of TTS models, Google's brand-new `gemini-3.1-flash-tts`, ElevenLabs v3, MiniMax 2.6 HD, Kokoro's multilingual voices, and more. Pass the model ID as a string literal for fully typed `modelOptions`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\n// Google Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS, 80+ languages, expressive audio tags\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: falSpeech('fal-ai/gemini-3.1-flash-tts'),\n  text: '[warm, enthusiastic] Welcome to TanStack AI!',\n  voice: 'Kore',\n})\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\n// Kokoro multilingual\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: falSpeech('fal-ai/kokoro/american-english'),\n  text: 'Hello from fal!',\n  voice: 'af_heart',\n  speed: 1.0,\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.audio) // Base64 encoded audio\nconsole.log(result.format) // e.g. \"wav\"\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\n// ElevenLabs v3 with model-specific options\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: falSpeech('fal-ai/elevenlabs/tts/eleven-v3'),\n  text: 'Welcome to TanStack AI.',\n  // The fal adapter maps top-level `voice`/`speed` into the model input;\n  // `modelOptions` is reserved for model-specific keys.\n  voice: 'Rachel',\n  modelOptions: {\n    stability: 0.5,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### BytePlus Seed Speech\n\nSeed Speech is a **separate BytePlus product from ModelArk**, so it uses its own key (`BYTEPLUS_VOICE_API_KEY`) rather than the `ARK_API_KEY` the chat, image and video adapters read. Voice ids go on the wire as Seed Speech's `speaker`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0'),\n  text: 'Welcome to TanStack AI!',\n  voice: 'en_female_stokie_uranus_bigtts',\n  format: 'mp3',\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.contentType) // \"audio/mpeg\"\n```\n\nFormats are `wav`, `mp3`, `pcm` and `ogg_opus`, and synthesis is **capped at 120 seconds of output**.\n\nSeed Audio also does multi-role dialogue and word-level timings. Use `turns` for dialogue and `timestamps` for timings, both covered below.\n\nSeed Speech has no top-level `speaker` field: the adapter sends `voice` as `references: [{ speaker }]`. Because `modelOptions.references` **replaces** that array rather than merging into it, passing `references` for voice cloning silently drops `voice` — include a `speaker` member yourself if you still want a stock voice. See the [BytePlus adapter](../adapters/byteplus#text-to-speech-seed-speech) for the voice-id naming conventions.\n\n## Options\n\n### Common Options\n\nAll TTS adapters support these common options:\n\n| Option | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `text` | `string` | The text to convert to speech. Required unless you pass `turns` |\n| `turns` | `Array<{ text, voice }>` | Dialogue lines, one per speaker turn. Use it instead of `text` |\n| `voice` | `string` | The voice to use for generation |\n| `format` | `string` | Output audio format (e.g., \"mp3\", \"wav\") |\n| `timestamps` | `boolean` | Ask for `alignment` and `segments` on the result |\n\n### OpenAI Voice Options\n\nOpenAI provides several distinct voices:\n\n| Voice | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `alloy` | Neutral, balanced voice |\n| `echo` | Warm, conversational voice |\n| `fable` | Expressive, storytelling voice |\n| `onyx` | Deep, authoritative voice |\n| `nova` | Friendly, upbeat voice |\n| `shimmer` | Clear, gentle voice |\n| `ash` | Calm, measured voice |\n| `ballad` | Melodic, flowing voice |\n| `coral` | Bright, energetic voice |\n| `sage` | Wise, thoughtful voice |\n| `verse` | Poetic, rhythmic voice |\n\n### OpenAI Format Options\n\n| Format | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `mp3` | MP3 audio (default) |\n| `opus` | Opus audio (good for streaming) |\n| `aac` | AAC audio |\n| `flac` | FLAC audio (lossless) |\n| `wav` | WAV audio (uncompressed) |\n| `pcm` | Raw PCM audio |\n\n## Dialogue With Two or More Voices\n\nYou want a two-person skit, and one `text` string with one `voice` cannot give\nyou that. Prefixing speaker names into the string is a guess about the prompt\nformat, and the provider never tells you which line landed where.\n\nPass `turns` instead. Each turn carries its own text and its own voice:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\n// Replace SECOND_VOICE with another voice id from the BytePlus voice list.\nconst SECOND_VOICE = 'your-second-voice-id'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0'),\n  turns: [\n    {\n      text: 'Do you have a left-handed bass?',\n      voice: 'en_female_stokie_uranus_bigtts',\n    },\n    { text: 'We do. Come and try it.', voice: SECOND_VOICE },\n  ],\n  format: 'mp3',\n})\n```\n\n`turns` and `text` are mutually exclusive. Pass one or the other.\n\nNot every provider can do dialogue, and the ones that can have different\nspeaker limits. The adapter declares its limit, so a request that asks for too\nmany voices fails before it reaches the provider:\n\n| Adapter | Distinct voices per request |\n|---------|------------------------------|\n| `byteplusSpeech` | 3 |\n| `elevenlabsSpeech` | 10 |\n| `geminiSpeech` | 2 |\n| Other TTS adapters | Dialogue not supported |\n\nRead the limit at runtime from `adapter.capabilities`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\nconst adapter = byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0')\n\nconsole.log(adapter.capabilities?.maxSpeakers) // 3\nconsole.log(adapter.capabilities?.timestamps) // true\n```\n\n## Timings: Where Each Word and Turn Lands\n\n`result.duration` is the length of the file. It does not tell you where speech\nstops, and it does not tell you which turn is where. Trimming trailing silence\nor captioning a clip needs both.\n\nSet `timestamps: true` and the result carries the timings:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0'),\n  text: 'Welcome to the guitar store.',\n  timestamps: true,\n})\n\n// Where speech ends, which is earlier than the end of the file.\nconst speechEnds = result.alignment?.endSeconds.at(-1)\n\nfor (const segment of result.segments ?? []) {\n  console.log(segment.startSeconds, segment.endSeconds, segment.text)\n}\n```\n\nTwo fields come back, and they answer different questions:\n\n- `alignment`: one entry per character or per word, with start and end times.\n  `alignment.unit` says which granularity the provider reported.\n- `segments`: one entry per turn (dialogue) or per sentence (single voice).\n  A dialogue segment also carries `turnIndex` and `voice`.\n\nAll times are seconds. Providers that report milliseconds convert in the\nadapter, so you never mix units.\n\n`timestamps` is rejected on an adapter that cannot return timings, rather than\nsilently giving you a result with nothing in it. Check\n`adapter.capabilities?.timestamps` before you ask.\n\n## Playing Audio in the Browser\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Convert base64 to audio and play\nfunction playAudio(result: TTSResult) {\n  const audioData = atob(result.audio)\n  const bytes = new Uint8Array(audioData.length)\n  for (let i = 0; i < audioData.length; i++) {\n    bytes[i] = audioData.charCodeAt(i)\n  }\n  \n  const blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: result.contentType })\n  const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)\n  \n  const audio = new Audio(url)\n  audio.play()\n  \n  // Clean up when done\n  audio.onended = () => URL.revokeObjectURL(url)\n}\n```\n\n## Saving Audio to File (Node.js)\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { writeFile } from 'fs/promises'\n\nasync function saveAudio(result: TTSResult, filename: string) {\n  const audioBuffer = Buffer.from(result.audio, 'base64')\n  await writeFile(filename, audioBuffer)\n  console.log(`Saved to ${filename}`)\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n  text: 'Hello world!',\n})\n\nawait saveAudio(result, 'output.mp3')\n```\n\n## Full-Stack Usage\n\nTanStack AI provides React hooks and server-side streaming helpers to build full-stack text-to-speech with minimal boilerplate.\n\n### Streaming Mode (Server Route + Client Hook)\n\n**Server**, Create an API route that wraps `generateSpeech` as a streaming response:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/generate/speech.ts\nimport { generateSpeech, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/generate/speech')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body = await request.json()\n        const { text, voice, format, model } = body.data\n\n        const stream = generateSpeech({\n          adapter: openaiSpeech(model ?? 'tts-1'),\n          text,\n          voice,\n          format,\n          stream: true,\n        })\n\n        return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n**Client**, Use the `useGenerateSpeech` hook with a connection adapter:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateSpeech, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/speech'),\n  })\n\n  const playAudio = () => {\n    if (!result) return\n    const audioData = atob(result.audio)\n    const bytes = new Uint8Array(audioData.length)\n    for (let i = 0; i < audioData.length; i++) {\n      bytes[i] = audioData.charCodeAt(i)\n    }\n    const blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: result.contentType })\n    const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)\n    const audio = new Audio(url)\n    audio.play()\n    audio.onended = () => URL.revokeObjectURL(url)\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate Speech'}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n      {result && <button onClick={playAudio}>Play Audio</button>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe other two transports (a server function returning JSON, or one returning an\nSSE `Response`) work the same way here. They are in\n[Advanced: other transports](#other-transports), and explained once in\n[Generations](./generations#transports-in-full).\n\n### Hook API\n\nThe `useGenerateSpeech` hook accepts:\n\n| Option | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `connection` | `ConnectionAdapter` | Streaming transport (SSE, HTTP stream, custom) |\n| `fetcher` | `(input) => Promise<TTSResult \\| Response>` | Direct async function, or server function returning an SSE `Response` |\n| `onResult` | `(result) => TOutput \\| null \\| void` | Callback when audio is generated. Optionally return a transformed value (see [Result Transform](#result-transform)) |\n| `onError` | `(error) => void` | Callback on error |\n| `onProgress` | `(progress, message?) => void` | Progress updates (0-100) |\n\nAnd returns:\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `generate` | `(input: SpeechGenerateInput) => Promise<void>` | Trigger generation |\n| `result` | `TOutput \\| null` | The result (or transformed result), or null |\n| `isLoading` | `boolean` | Whether generation is in progress |\n| `error` | `Error \\| undefined` | Current error, if any |\n| `status` | `GenerationClientState` | `'idle'` \\| `'generating'` \\| `'success'` \\| `'error'` |\n| `stop` | `() => void` | Abort the current generation |\n| `reset` | `() => void` | Clear result, error, and return to idle |\n\n### Result Transform\n\nThe `onResult` callback can optionally return a transformed value that replaces the stored `result`. This is useful for converting raw API responses into a more convenient format for your components.\n\n**Transform behavior:**\n- Return a **non-null value** to replace the stored result with the transformed value\n- Return **`null`** to keep the previous result unchanged (useful for filtering)\n- Return **nothing** (`void`) to store the raw result as-is (backward compatible)\n\n**Example: Convert base64 audio to a playable Audio element**\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateSpeech, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport type { TTSResult } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nfunction SpeechPlayer() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/speech'),\n    onResult: (raw: TTSResult) => {\n      const audioData = atob(raw.audio)\n      const bytes = new Uint8Array(audioData.length)\n      for (let i = 0; i < audioData.length; i++) {\n        bytes[i] = audioData.charCodeAt(i)\n      }\n      const blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: raw.contentType })\n      const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)\n      return {\n        audio: new Audio(url),\n        duration: raw.duration,\n      }\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello world!', voice: 'alloy' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n      {result && (\n        <button onClick={() => result.audio.play()}>\n          Play Audio\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nTypeScript automatically infers the result type from your `onResult` return value, no explicit generic parameter needed. In this example, `result` is inferred as `{ audio: HTMLAudioElement; duration?: number } | null`, so `result.audio.play()` is fully type-safe.\n\n## Advanced\n\nReference detail you do not need to get this working.\n\n### Other transports\n\n#### Direct Mode (Server Function + Fetcher)\n\nFor non-streaming usage with TanStack Start server functions:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport const generateSpeechFn = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .inputValidator((data: { text: string; voice?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    return generateSpeech({\n      adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n      text: data.text,\n      voice: data.voice,\n    })\n  })\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { generateSpeechFn } from '../lib/server-functions'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    fetcher: (input) => generateSpeechFn({ data: input }),\n  })\n  // ... same UI as above\n}\n```\n\n#### Server Function Streaming (Fetcher + Response)\n\nFor TanStack Start server functions that stream results. The fetcher receives type-safe input and returns an SSE `Response`, the client parses it automatically:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { generateSpeech, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport const generateSpeechStreamFn = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .inputValidator((data: { text: string; voice?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(({ data }) => {\n    return toServerSentEventsResponse(\n      generateSpeech({\n        adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n        text: data.text,\n        voice: data.voice,\n        stream: true,\n      }),\n    )\n  })\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { generateSpeechStreamFn } from '../lib/server-functions'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    fetcher: (input) => generateSpeechStreamFn({ data: input }),\n  })\n  // ... same UI as above\n}\n```\n\n### Model Options\n\n#### OpenAI Model Options\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1-hd'),\n  text: 'High quality speech synthesis',\n  voice: 'nova',\n  format: 'mp3',\n  speed: 1.0, // top-level option, 0.25 to 4.0\n  modelOptions: {\n    instructions: 'Speak in a calm, measured tone', // GPT-4o audio models only\n  },\n})\n```\n\n> **Note:** `voice`, `format`, and `speed` are top-level `generateSpeech` options, not `modelOptions` keys.\n\n| Option | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `instructions` | `string` | Voice style instructions (GPT-4o audio models only) |\n\n> **Note:** The `instructions` and `stream_format` options are only available with the `gpt-4o-audio-preview` model, not with `tts-1` or `tts-1-hd`.\n\n### Response Format\n\nThe TTS result includes:\n\n```typescript ignore\ninterface TTSResult {\n  id: string        // Unique identifier for this generation\n  model: string     // The model used\n  audio: string     // Base64-encoded audio data\n  format: string    // Audio format (e.g., \"mp3\")\n  contentType: string // MIME type (e.g., \"audio/mpeg\")\n  duration?: number // Duration in seconds (if available)\n}\n```\n\n### Model Availability\n\n#### OpenAI Models\n\n| Model | Quality | Speed | Use Case |\n|-------|---------|-------|----------|\n| `tts-1` | Standard | Fast | Real-time applications |\n| `tts-1-hd` | High | Slower | Production audio |\n| `gpt-4o-audio-preview` | Highest | Variable | Advanced voice control |\n\n#### Gemini Models\n\n| Model | Status | Notes |\n|-------|--------|-------|\n| `gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts` | Experimental | May require Live API for full features |\n\n### Error Handling\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\ntry {\n  const result = await generateSpeech({\n    adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n    text: 'Hello!',\n  })\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    if (error.message.includes('exceeds maximum length')) {\n      console.error('Text is too long (max 4096 characters)')\n    } else if (error.message.includes('Speed must be between')) {\n      console.error('Invalid speed value')\n    } else {\n      console.error('TTS error:', error.message)\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n> **Tip:** To trigger speech generation from your frontend with loading states, see [Generation Hooks](./generation-hooks).\n\n> **Debugging:** When a TTS request fails or produces unexpected output, pass `debug: true` on `generateSpeech({...})` to log the outgoing request, every raw provider chunk, and any caught error. See [Debug Logging](../advanced/debug-logging).\n\n### Environment Variables\n\nThe TTS adapters use the same environment variables as other adapters:\n\n- **OpenAI**: `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n- **Gemini**: `GOOGLE_API_KEY` or `GEMINI_API_KEY`\n- **BytePlus**: `BYTEPLUS_VOICE_API_KEY` (Seed Speech is a different product from ModelArk — the `ARK_API_KEY` used by the chat/image/video adapters is not accepted here)\n\n### Explicit API Keys\n\nFor production use or when you need explicit control:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOpenaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { createGeminiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n\n// OpenAI\nconst openaiAdapter = createOpenaiSpeech('tts-1', 'your-openai-api-key')\n\n// Gemini\nconst geminiAdapter = createGeminiSpeech('gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview', 'your-google-api-key')\n```\n\n### Best Practices\n\n1. **Text Length**: OpenAI TTS supports up to 4096 characters per request. For longer content, split into chunks.\n\n2. **Voice Selection**: Choose voices appropriate for your content—use `onyx` for authoritative content, `nova` for friendly interactions.\n\n3. **Format Selection**: Use `mp3` for general use, `opus` for streaming, `wav` for further processing.\n\n4. **Caching**: Cache generated audio to avoid regenerating the same content.\n\n5. **Error Handling**: Always handle errors gracefully, especially for user-facing applications.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Text-to-Speech\nid: text-to-speech\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Convert text to spoken audio with OpenAI TTS, Gemini voice models, and BytePlus Seed Speech via TanStack AI's generateSpeech() API.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - text-to-speech\n  - tts\n  - generateSpeech\n  - openai tts\n  - voice synthesis\n  - speech generation\n---\n\nTanStack AI provides support for text-to-speech generation through dedicated TTS adapters. This guide covers how to convert text into spoken audio using OpenAI and Gemini providers.\n\n## Overview\n\nText-to-speech (TTS) is handled by TTS adapters that follow the same tree-shakeable architecture as other adapters in TanStack AI. The TTS adapters support:\n\n- **OpenAI**: TTS-1, TTS-1-HD, and audio-capable GPT-4o models\n- **Gemini**: Gemini 2.5 Flash TTS (experimental)\n- **BytePlus**: Seed Speech (`seed-audio-1.0`)\n- **fal.ai**: Kokoro, ElevenLabs, MiniMax, Chatterbox, Dia, Orpheus, F5-TTS, VibeVoice, and more\n\nMost providers here ship a fixed catalog of voices. When none of them fit, [create your own](./voice-creation) and pass the new voice ID as `voice`. On a provider whose catalog is per-account, `listVoices()` reads back what is available.\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n### OpenAI Text-to-Speech\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\n// Generate speech from text (uses OPENAI_API_KEY from environment)\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n  text: 'Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!',\n  voice: 'alloy',\n})\n\n// result.audio contains base64-encoded audio data\nconsole.log(result.format) // 'mp3'\nconsole.log(result.contentType) // 'audio/mpeg'\n```\n\n### Gemini Text-to-Speech (Experimental)\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { geminiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n\n// Generate speech from text (uses GOOGLE_API_KEY or GEMINI_API_KEY from environment)\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: geminiSpeech('gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview'),\n  text: 'Hello from Gemini TTS!',\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.audio) // Base64 encoded audio\n```\n\n### fal.ai Text-to-Speech\n\nfal.ai offers a broad selection of TTS models, Google's brand-new `gemini-3.1-flash-tts`, ElevenLabs v3, MiniMax 2.6 HD, Kokoro's multilingual voices, and more. Pass the model ID as a string literal for fully typed `modelOptions`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\n// Google Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS, 80+ languages, expressive audio tags\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: falSpeech('fal-ai/gemini-3.1-flash-tts'),\n  text: '[warm, enthusiastic] Welcome to TanStack AI!',\n  voice: 'Kore',\n})\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\n// Kokoro multilingual\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: falSpeech('fal-ai/kokoro/american-english'),\n  text: 'Hello from fal!',\n  voice: 'af_heart',\n  speed: 1.0,\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.audio) // Base64 encoded audio\nconsole.log(result.format) // e.g. \"wav\"\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\n// ElevenLabs v3 with model-specific options\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: falSpeech('fal-ai/elevenlabs/tts/eleven-v3'),\n  text: 'Welcome to TanStack AI.',\n  // The fal adapter maps top-level `voice`/`speed` into the model input;\n  // `modelOptions` is reserved for model-specific keys.\n  voice: 'Rachel',\n  modelOptions: {\n    stability: 0.5,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### BytePlus Seed Speech\n\nSeed Speech is a **separate BytePlus product from ModelArk**, so it uses its own key (`BYTEPLUS_VOICE_API_KEY`) rather than the `ARK_API_KEY` the chat, image and video adapters read. Voice ids go on the wire as Seed Speech's `speaker`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0'),\n  text: 'Welcome to TanStack AI!',\n  voice: 'en_female_stokie_uranus_bigtts',\n  format: 'mp3',\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.contentType) // \"audio/mpeg\"\n```\n\nFormats are `wav`, `mp3`, `pcm` and `ogg_opus`, and synthesis is **capped at 120 seconds of output**.\n\nSeed Audio also does multi-role dialogue and word-level timings. Use `turns` for dialogue and `timestamps` for timings, both covered below.\n\nSeed Speech has no top-level `speaker` field: the adapter sends `voice` as `references: [{ speaker }]`. Because `modelOptions.references` **replaces** that array rather than merging into it, passing `references` for voice cloning silently drops `voice` — include a `speaker` member yourself if you still want a stock voice. See the [BytePlus adapter](../adapters/byteplus#text-to-speech-seed-speech) for the voice-id naming conventions.\n\n## Options\n\n### Common Options\n\nAll TTS adapters support these common options:\n\n| Option | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `text` | `string` | The text to convert to speech. Required unless you pass `turns` |\n| `turns` | `Array<{ text, voice }>` | Dialogue lines, one per speaker turn. Use it instead of `text` |\n| `voice` | `string` | The voice to use for generation |\n| `format` | `string` | Output audio format (e.g., \"mp3\", \"wav\") |\n| `timestamps` | `boolean` | Ask for `alignment` and `segments` on the result |\n\n### OpenAI Voice Options\n\nOpenAI provides several distinct voices:\n\n| Voice | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `alloy` | Neutral, balanced voice |\n| `echo` | Warm, conversational voice |\n| `fable` | Expressive, storytelling voice |\n| `onyx` | Deep, authoritative voice |\n| `nova` | Friendly, upbeat voice |\n| `shimmer` | Clear, gentle voice |\n| `ash` | Calm, measured voice |\n| `ballad` | Melodic, flowing voice |\n| `coral` | Bright, energetic voice |\n| `sage` | Wise, thoughtful voice |\n| `verse` | Poetic, rhythmic voice |\n\n### OpenAI Format Options\n\n| Format | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `mp3` | MP3 audio (default) |\n| `opus` | Opus audio (good for streaming) |\n| `aac` | AAC audio |\n| `flac` | FLAC audio (lossless) |\n| `wav` | WAV audio (uncompressed) |\n| `pcm` | Raw PCM audio |\n\n## Dialogue With Two or More Voices\n\nYou want a two-person skit, and one `text` string with one `voice` cannot give\nyou that. Prefixing speaker names into the string is a guess about the prompt\nformat, and the provider never tells you which line landed where.\n\nPass `turns` instead. Each turn carries its own text and its own voice:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\n// Replace SECOND_VOICE with another voice id from the BytePlus voice list.\nconst SECOND_VOICE = 'your-second-voice-id'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0'),\n  turns: [\n    {\n      text: 'Do you have a left-handed bass?',\n      voice: 'en_female_stokie_uranus_bigtts',\n    },\n    { text: 'We do. Come and try it.', voice: SECOND_VOICE },\n  ],\n  format: 'mp3',\n})\n```\n\n`turns` and `text` are mutually exclusive. Pass one or the other.\n\nNot every provider can do dialogue, and the ones that can have different\nspeaker limits. The adapter declares its limit, so a request that asks for too\nmany voices fails before it reaches the provider:\n\n| Adapter | Distinct voices per request |\n|---------|------------------------------|\n| `byteplusSpeech` | 3 |\n| `elevenlabsSpeech` | 10 |\n| `geminiSpeech` | 2 |\n| Other TTS adapters | Dialogue not supported |\n\nRead the limit at runtime from `adapter.capabilities`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\nconst adapter = byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0')\n\nconsole.log(adapter.capabilities?.maxSpeakers) // 3\nconsole.log(adapter.capabilities?.timestamps) // true\n```\n\n## Timings: Where Each Word and Turn Lands\n\n`result.duration` is the length of the file. It does not tell you where speech\nstops, and it does not tell you which turn is where. Trimming trailing silence\nor captioning a clip needs both.\n\nSet `timestamps: true` and the result carries the timings:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { byteplusSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-byteplus'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: byteplusSpeech('seed-audio-1.0'),\n  text: 'Welcome to the guitar store.',\n  timestamps: true,\n})\n\n// Where speech ends, which is earlier than the end of the file.\nconst speechEnds = result.alignment?.endSeconds.at(-1)\n\nfor (const segment of result.segments ?? []) {\n  console.log(segment.startSeconds, segment.endSeconds, segment.text)\n}\n```\n\nTwo fields come back, and they answer different questions:\n\n- `alignment`: one entry per character or per word, with start and end times.\n  `alignment.unit` says which granularity the provider reported.\n- `segments`: one entry per turn (dialogue) or per sentence (single voice).\n  A dialogue segment also carries `turnIndex` and `voice`.\n\nAll times are seconds. Providers that report milliseconds convert in the\nadapter, so you never mix units.\n\n`timestamps` is rejected on an adapter that cannot return timings, rather than\nsilently giving you a result with nothing in it. Check\n`adapter.capabilities?.timestamps` before you ask.\n\n## Playing Audio in the Browser\n\n```typescript ignore\n// Convert base64 to audio and play\nfunction playAudio(result: TTSResult) {\n  const audioData = atob(result.audio)\n  const bytes = new Uint8Array(audioData.length)\n  for (let i = 0; i < audioData.length; i++) {\n    bytes[i] = audioData.charCodeAt(i)\n  }\n  \n  const blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: result.contentType })\n  const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)\n  \n  const audio = new Audio(url)\n  audio.play()\n  \n  // Clean up when done\n  audio.onended = () => URL.revokeObjectURL(url)\n}\n```\n\n## Saving Audio to File (Node.js)\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { writeFile } from 'fs/promises'\n\nasync function saveAudio(result: TTSResult, filename: string) {\n  const audioBuffer = Buffer.from(result.audio, 'base64')\n  await writeFile(filename, audioBuffer)\n  console.log(`Saved to ${filename}`)\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n  text: 'Hello world!',\n})\n\nawait saveAudio(result, 'output.mp3')\n```\n\n## Full-Stack Usage\n\nTanStack AI provides React hooks and server-side streaming helpers to build full-stack text-to-speech with minimal boilerplate.\n\n### Streaming Mode (Server Route + Client Hook)\n\n**Server**, Create an API route that wraps `generateSpeech` as a streaming response:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/generate/speech.ts\nimport { generateSpeech, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/generate/speech')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body = await request.json()\n        const { text, voice, format, model } = body.data\n\n        const stream = generateSpeech({\n          adapter: openaiSpeech(model ?? 'tts-1'),\n          text,\n          voice,\n          format,\n          stream: true,\n        })\n\n        return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n**Client**, Use the `useGenerateSpeech` hook with a connection adapter:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateSpeech, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading, error } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/speech'),\n  })\n\n  const playAudio = () => {\n    if (!result) return\n    const audioData = atob(result.audio)\n    const bytes = new Uint8Array(audioData.length)\n    for (let i = 0; i < audioData.length; i++) {\n      bytes[i] = audioData.charCodeAt(i)\n    }\n    const blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: result.contentType })\n    const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)\n    const audio = new Audio(url)\n    audio.play()\n    audio.onended = () => URL.revokeObjectURL(url)\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello, welcome to TanStack AI!' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        {isLoading ? 'Generating...' : 'Generate Speech'}\n      </button>\n      {error && <p>Error: {error.message}</p>}\n      {result && <button onClick={playAudio}>Play Audio</button>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe other two transports (a server function returning JSON, or one returning an\nSSE `Response`) work the same way here. They are in\n[Advanced: other transports](#other-transports), and explained once in\n[Generations](./generations#transports-in-full).\n\n### Hook API\n\nThe `useGenerateSpeech` hook accepts:\n\n| Option | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `connection` | `ConnectionAdapter` | Streaming transport (SSE, HTTP stream, custom) |\n| `fetcher` | `(input) => Promise<TTSResult \\| Response>` | Direct async function, or server function returning an SSE `Response` |\n| `onResult` | `(result) => TOutput \\| null \\| void` | Callback when audio is generated. Optionally return a transformed value (see [Result Transform](#result-transform)) |\n| `onError` | `(error) => void` | Callback on error |\n| `onProgress` | `(progress, message?) => void` | Progress updates (0-100) |\n\nAnd returns:\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| `generate` | `(input: SpeechGenerateInput) => Promise<void>` | Trigger generation |\n| `result` | `TOutput \\| null` | The result (or transformed result), or null |\n| `isLoading` | `boolean` | Whether generation is in progress |\n| `error` | `Error \\| undefined` | Current error, if any |\n| `status` | `GenerationClientState` | `'idle'` \\| `'generating'` \\| `'success'` \\| `'error'` |\n| `stop` | `() => void` | Abort the current generation |\n| `reset` | `() => void` | Clear result, error, and return to idle |\n\n### Result Transform\n\nThe `onResult` callback can optionally return a transformed value that replaces the stored `result`. This is useful for converting raw API responses into a more convenient format for your components.\n\n**Transform behavior:**\n- Return a **non-null value** to replace the stored result with the transformed value\n- Return **`null`** to keep the previous result unchanged (useful for filtering)\n- Return **nothing** (`void`) to store the raw result as-is (backward compatible)\n\n**Example: Convert base64 audio to a playable Audio element**\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateSpeech, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport type { TTSResult } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nfunction SpeechPlayer() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/generate/speech'),\n    onResult: (raw: TTSResult) => {\n      const audioData = atob(raw.audio)\n      const bytes = new Uint8Array(audioData.length)\n      for (let i = 0; i < audioData.length; i++) {\n        bytes[i] = audioData.charCodeAt(i)\n      }\n      const blob = new Blob([bytes], { type: raw.contentType })\n      const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)\n      return {\n        audio: new Audio(url),\n        duration: raw.duration,\n      }\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button\n        onClick={() => generate({ text: 'Hello world!', voice: 'alloy' })}\n        disabled={isLoading}\n      >\n        Generate\n      </button>\n      {result && (\n        <button onClick={() => result.audio.play()}>\n          Play Audio\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nTypeScript automatically infers the result type from your `onResult` return value, no explicit generic parameter needed. In this example, `result` is inferred as `{ audio: HTMLAudioElement; duration?: number } | null`, so `result.audio.play()` is fully type-safe.\n\n## Advanced\n\nReference detail you do not need to get this working.\n\n### Other transports\n\n#### Direct Mode (Server Function + Fetcher)\n\nFor non-streaming usage with TanStack Start server functions:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport const generateSpeechFn = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .inputValidator((data: { text: string; voice?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(async ({ data }) => {\n    return generateSpeech({\n      adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n      text: data.text,\n      voice: data.voice,\n    })\n  })\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { generateSpeechFn } from '../lib/server-functions'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    fetcher: (input) => generateSpeechFn({ data: input }),\n  })\n  // ... same UI as above\n}\n```\n\n#### Server Function Streaming (Fetcher + Response)\n\nFor TanStack Start server functions that stream results. The fetcher receives type-safe input and returns an SSE `Response`, the client parses it automatically:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// lib/server-functions.ts\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport { generateSpeech, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nexport const generateSpeechStreamFn = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .inputValidator((data: { text: string; voice?: string }) => data)\n  .handler(({ data }) => {\n    return toServerSentEventsResponse(\n      generateSpeech({\n        adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n        text: data.text,\n        voice: data.voice,\n        stream: true,\n      }),\n    )\n  })\n```\n\n```tsx\nimport { useGenerateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { generateSpeechStreamFn } from '../lib/server-functions'\n\nfunction SpeechGenerator() {\n  const { generate, result, isLoading } = useGenerateSpeech({\n    fetcher: (input) => generateSpeechStreamFn({ data: input }),\n  })\n  // ... same UI as above\n}\n```\n\n### Model Options\n\n#### OpenAI Model Options\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst result = await generateSpeech({\n  adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1-hd'),\n  text: 'High quality speech synthesis',\n  voice: 'nova',\n  format: 'mp3',\n  speed: 1.0, // top-level option, 0.25 to 4.0\n  modelOptions: {\n    instructions: 'Speak in a calm, measured tone', // GPT-4o audio models only\n  },\n})\n```\n\n> **Note:** `voice`, `format`, and `speed` are top-level `generateSpeech` options, not `modelOptions` keys.\n\n| Option | Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| `instructions` | `string` | Voice style instructions (GPT-4o audio models only) |\n\n> **Note:** The `instructions` and `stream_format` options are only available with the `gpt-4o-audio-preview` model, not with `tts-1` or `tts-1-hd`.\n\n### Response Format\n\nThe TTS result includes:\n\n```typescript ignore\ninterface TTSResult {\n  id: string        // Unique identifier for this generation\n  model: string     // The model used\n  audio: string     // Base64-encoded audio data\n  format: string    // Audio format (e.g., \"mp3\")\n  contentType: string // MIME type (e.g., \"audio/mpeg\")\n  duration?: number // Duration in seconds (if available)\n}\n```\n\n### Model Availability\n\n#### OpenAI Models\n\n| Model | Quality | Speed | Use Case |\n|-------|---------|-------|----------|\n| `tts-1` | Standard | Fast | Real-time applications |\n| `tts-1-hd` | High | Slower | Production audio |\n| `gpt-4o-audio-preview` | Highest | Variable | Advanced voice control |\n\n#### Gemini Models\n\n| Model | Status | Notes |\n|-------|--------|-------|\n| `gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts` | Experimental | May require Live API for full features |\n\n### Error Handling\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\ntry {\n  const result = await generateSpeech({\n    adapter: openaiSpeech('tts-1'),\n    text: 'Hello!',\n  })\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    if (error.message.includes('exceeds maximum length')) {\n      console.error('Text is too long (max 4096 characters)')\n    } else if (error.message.includes('Speed must be between')) {\n      console.error('Invalid speed value')\n    } else {\n      console.error('TTS error:', error.message)\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n> **Tip:** To trigger speech generation from your frontend with loading states, see [Generation Hooks](./generation-hooks).\n\n> **Debugging:** When a TTS request fails or produces unexpected output, pass `debug: true` on `generateSpeech({...})` to log the outgoing request, every raw provider chunk, and any caught error. See [Debug Logging](../advanced/debug-logging).\n\n### Environment Variables\n\nThe TTS adapters use the same environment variables as other adapters:\n\n- **OpenAI**: `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n- **Gemini**: `GOOGLE_API_KEY` or `GEMINI_API_KEY`\n- **BytePlus**: `BYTEPLUS_VOICE_API_KEY` (Seed Speech is a different product from ModelArk — the `ARK_API_KEY` used by the chat/image/video adapters is not accepted here)\n\n### Explicit API Keys\n\nFor production use or when you need explicit control:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOpenaiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { createGeminiSpeech } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\n\n// OpenAI\nconst openaiAdapter = createOpenaiSpeech('tts-1', 'your-openai-api-key')\n\n// Gemini\nconst geminiAdapter = createGeminiSpeech('gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview', 'your-google-api-key')\n```\n\n### Best Practices\n\n1. **Text Length**: OpenAI TTS supports up to 4096 characters per request. For longer content, split into chunks.\n\n2. **Voice Selection**: Choose voices appropriate for your content—use `onyx` for authoritative content, `nova` for friendly interactions.\n\n3. **Format Selection**: Use `mp3` for general use, `opus` for streaming, `wav` for further processing.\n\n4. **Caching**: Cache generated audio to avoid regenerating the same content.\n\n5. **Error Handling**: Always handle errors gracefully, especially for user-facing applications.\n"}
